{
  "_comment": [
    "claude.listModels is a CATALOG method: it is in the brain's catalogMethods()",
    "and the desktop registers it through cat(), which is a no-op under the default",
    "DELEGATE_CATALOG_TO_BRAIN. So the brain answers it for every web, mobile,",
    "remote and MCP client while the desktop IPC path serves its own copy — and the",
    "two answered a DIFFERENT CONTRACT, each pinned by its own suite:",
    "",
    "  aliases                4 rows here, 6 there. opus[1m] and sonnet[1m] — the",
    "                         million-token-context ids — were simply unreachable",
    "                         from the web picker.",
    "  labels                 'Opus — latest' vs the version-stamped 'Opus 4.5'.",
    "  context                absent entirely on one side; it is the 200K/1M badge.",
    "  defaultPermissionMode  absent entirely on one side, so the mode remembered",
    "                         from the last spawn was lost on that path.",
    "  seen                   one side offered Claude Code's internal '<synthetic>'",
    "                         placeholder as a selectable model id, and neither",
    "                         absorbed the newest-per-family duplicate.",
    "",
    "`config` is the config.yaml `claude` section; `live` is the model ids observed",
    "in claudemon's live sessions (session.usage.model), which both copies merge in.",
    "`expected` is the whole reply, field for field and in order."
  ],
  "vocabulary": {
    "_comment": [
      "THE BLOCK REGISTRY. Every array-of-objects block in this file must be declared",
      "here and everything here must be a block — closure in both directions, so a new",
      "block is a failure until someone says what its cases must carry, and a renamed",
      "one cannot quietly stop being validated.",
      "",
      "Held by cmd/brain/corpusvocab_test.go and",
      "apps/desktop/src/main/services/contractsVocabulary.test.ts. Before those, this",
      "kind of validation existed for exactly ONE block of ONE fixture."
    ],
    "blocks": {
      "cases": {
        "why": "claude.listModels' catalog answer for a config + live-snapshot pair.",
        "required": ["name", "config", "live", "expected", "why"],
        "loaders": [
          "services/hub/cmd/brain/models_contract_test.go::TestClaudeModelCatalogContractCases(",
          "apps/desktop/src/main/services/claudeModelCatalogContract.test.ts::contracts/claude-model-catalog-cases.json"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no models seen at all: bare alias labels, empty seen",
      "config": {
        "defaultModel": "",
        "contextWindow": null,
        "skipPermissionsDefault": false,
        "defaultPermissionMode": "",
        "seenModels": []
      },
      "live": [],
      "expected": {
        "defaultModel": "",
        "contextWindow": null,
        "skipPermissionsDefault": false,
        "defaultPermissionMode": "",
        "aliases": [
          {
            "model": "fable",
            "value": "fable",
            "label": "Fable",
            "contextWindow": 1000000,
            "context": "1M"
          },
          {
            "model": "opus",
            "value": "opus",
            "label": "Opus",
            "contextWindow": 200000,
            "context": "200K"
          },
          {
            "model": "opus",
            "value": "opus[1m]",
            "label": "Opus",
            "contextWindow": 1000000,
            "context": "1M"
          },
          {
            "model": "sonnet",
            "value": "sonnet",
            "label": "Sonnet",
            "contextWindow": 200000,
            "context": "200K"
          },
          {
            "model": "sonnet",
            "value": "sonnet[1m]",
            "label": "Sonnet",
            "contextWindow": 1000000,
            "context": "1M"
          },
          {
            "model": "haiku",
            "value": "haiku",
            "label": "Haiku",
            "contextWindow": 200000,
            "context": "200K"
          }
        ],
        "seen": []
      },
      "why": "The floor, and the shape: SIX alias rows, each with a context badge. The Go copy shipped four rows labelled 'Opus — latest' and no context field at all, so the 1M-context ids opus[1m] and sonnet[1m] were unreachable from every web/mobile/remote picker — and the brain is the DEFAULT answerer for this method."
    },
    {
